  "body": "**Research note (bit headroom only); no \u03ba claim.** This answers an open question from [#2423](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2423): what is each further width-8 helper deletion worth on the bit supplier, once the freed slack is re-hosted optimally while respecting stage windows? [#1043](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1043)'s R438 is d = 1. #1250 shows that helper 470 is the only removable helper on the fixed word, so d \u2265 2 prices *changed* words.\n\n| d | R | slack S | certified optimum (unique) | c TEMPLATE (#1043's measured delta) | vs #589 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 439 | 45 | 9\u00d7(42,5) | 0.001733427039589844234749 | 0 |\n| 1 | 438 | 54 | 10\u00d7(42,5)+1\u00d7(42,4) | 0.001734802047828389852783 | +0.079% |\n| 2 | 437 | 63 | 12\u00d7(42,5)+1\u00d7(28,3) | 0.001736238589146810207048 | +0.162% |\n| 3 | 436 | 72 | 14\u00d7(42,5)+1\u00d7(28,2) | 0.001737652736279473456500 | +0.244% |\n| 4 | 435 | 81 | 16\u00d7(42,5)+1\u00d7(14,1) | 0.001739118212671177105905 | +0.328% |\n| 5 | 434 | 90 | 18\u00d7(42,5) | 0.001740604775296424266918 | +0.414% |\n| 6 | 433 | 99 | 19\u00d7(42,5)+1\u00d7(42,4) | 0.001741991196114600260000 | +0.494% |\n\n**Shape of the result.**\n- About **+0.082% c per deletion**, nearly linear. The steps alternate with S mod 5, which sets the partial slot.\n- The optimum is always fully idle 42-slots first, with one partial slot.\n- Two more illustrative per-deletion models are reported, RANK1 {1:\u22128} and RANK7 {7:\u22121, 1:\u22121}. Neither is an envelope, as the README explains.\n\n**How it was checked** (`deletion_ladder.py`, reusing the pinned verify_rehost machinery of #2423):\n- **Layouts:** an exact top-3 DP, cross-checked by exhaustive enumeration for every row (up to 728,466,365 layouts at d = 6).\n- **Windows:** all window splits are feasible by max-flow and by Hall, and the placements are audited.\n- **Endpoints:** 21 certified endpoints, each accepted at c and rejected at c + 1e-24.\n- **Controls:** the run reproduces the endpoints of #589 (d = 0), #1043's certified profile and #2423's re-hosting (d = 1), and #2423's transported word (d = 1, RANK7). It has 88 negative controls.\n- **Independent check:** an adversarial AI verifier recomputed all 21 rows with its own code (exhaustive layouts, Decimal endpoint bisection, a 512-subset Hall test) and matched every digit. Its three presentation fixes are applied.\n- **Packaging:** `--check-only`, the 3.10 grammar check and the research tests pass. Run on CPython 3.14.4; the registered 3.12 replay was not run.\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/bit-deletion-ladder/deletion_ladder.py --check research/bit-deletion-ladder/RECEIPT.json   # ~80 s\n# PASS_BIT_DELETION_LADDER d=0..6 exhaustive=21/21 windows_feasible=7/7 c_template(d=6)=0.001741991196114600260000 ... no_new_kappa\n```\n\n**Scope.**\n- No word exists for d \u2265 2, so the local models are declared rather than derived.\n- W, the #589 frames and the windows are held fixed.\n- The slot model is width-8 only, with no banks.\n- The native lane was not run.\n- The bit supplier does not bind \u03ba.\n- Base: main `0fdd7d82`. Card `selected-packing`, scope changed; the assignment is the bit-supplier track, seed 14.\n\n**Credits.**\n- #1043 (Ali Romman).\n- #2423 (this author).\n- #1023.\n- The seed72 and seed14 packages.\n- #589 / #555.\n- #1250 / bit-source-substitution-seed11.\n\nPrepared with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5): an AI builder and an adversarial AI verifier. No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
